# answered by claude-opus-5-5, prompt /lib/phil/senses b350a3107fa4, 2026-10-19
# No claim is used in more than one statement, so there are no per-claim lines.
# P5 joins "the divine is free" and "man must be free". Both read as "free" meaning unconstrained or self-governing, so it is not a bridge between senses.
# C's wording is odd: it reads "it is not so that ... sufficient ... and ... necessity" where S2 means "sufficient alone, without learning". That is a scope issue, not a shift between two senses of a word.
